The '''October 2026 Diet emergency resolution on the Wolffrean War''' (アドラ共同体第4942E号決議案に対する緊急決議) was an emergency resolution adopted by the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken]] on 27 October 2026, two days after the conclusion of the [[October 2026 Diet debate on the Wolffrean War|October emergency debate]]. The extraordinary session was convened in response to the submission of draft [[Adonian Community Resolution 4942E]], a [[Sindewand]]-sponsored text proposing the condemnation of [[Okaiken]] for its Pfein Sea escort operations, economic sanctions on the state, and personal sanctions — asset freezes and travel bans — on Prime Minister [[Kousuke Ikazaki]].

The resolution rejected the draft's characterisation of the escort flotilla as the use of military force outside international law, declared the proposed personal sanctions against a sitting head of government to be an interference in the democratic processes of a member state, and directed the government to press for the adoption of Okaiken's own draft [[Adonian Community Resolution 4942D]] establishing deconfliction zones for civilian shipping in the [[Pfein Sea]]. It passed 437–18 with 16 abstentions — the broadest cross-party majority recorded by the [[61st Diet of Okaiken|61st Diet]] — with only the [[Okaiken Innovation Party]] voting against.

== Background ==
{{Main|October 2026 Diet debate on the Wolffrean War|Adonian Community Resolution 4942E}}

On 24–25 October 2026, the House of Commoners had adopted the October Maritime Security and Non-Belligerence Legislative Package, which enacted statutory defensive rules of engagement for the [[Sanese Imperial Forces|SIF]] Escort Flotilla deployed to [[Alwana]] and gave parliamentary ratification to Okaiken's diplomatic promotion of draft Resolution 4942D. The flotilla — two destroyers including the ''[[ISN Shirakumo]]'' and an auxiliary replenishment vessel — was escorting eleven Sanese-flagged commercial ferries chartered by the [[Adonian Community]] for the civilian evacuation under [[Adonian Community Resolution 4935]], operating under the defensive provisions of the [[Kurosawa Doctrine]] and remaining under sovereign national command.

On 24 October, the same day the emergency debate opened in Okami, the delegation of Sindewand submitted draft Resolution 4942E to the [[Adonian Assembly]]. The draft proposed the condemnation of Okaiken for the authorisation of the escort deployment and of the rules of engagement enacted by the Emergency Maritime Civilian Protection Act, general economic sanctions on the state, and personal sanctions on the Prime Minister. It was referred to the [[Committee on Resolutions]] on the day of its submission. Under the legislative procedure of the Assembly, the draft would enter discussion only if approved by the Committee or co-sponsored by twenty member states.

The submission was widely read in Okami as a response to the vote of 28 September 2026, at which Okaiken's abstention had contributed to the defeat of draft Resolution 4936, which had proposed sanctions on Sindewand over its border closures to [[White Wolffrean]] populations. The Sindewand text itself invoked that abstention, arguing that Okaiken had undermined the consensus principle of Assembly missions. Confirmation of the referral reached the Sanese delegation on 26 October, and the Speaker convened an extraordinary session of the House of Commoners for the following morning on the government's request.

== The resolution ==

The resolution was tabled jointly by the leaders of the five governing and opposition parties represented in the chamber's business committee, an arrangement without precedent in the 61st Diet. Its formal title was the '''Resolution concerning the Government's Response to Draft Adonian Community Resolution 4942E and the Continued Promotion of Draft Resolution 4942D''' (アドラ共同体第4942E号決議案に対する政府方針及び第4942D号決議案の推進に関する緊急決議). Its operative paragraphs provided:

# Reaffirming that the escort flotilla operates under the humanitarian mandate of Resolution 4935 and remains under sovereign national command in accordance with the Kurosawa Doctrine;
# Declaring that the statutory rules of engagement enacted by the Emergency Maritime Civilian Protection Act are strictly defensive, comprising the interception of incoming ordnance and return fire against shore batteries actively firing on convoys within a fifteen-nautical-mile radius;
# Rejecting the characterisation, advanced in draft Resolution 4942E, of the deployment as the use of military force outside international law or outside the mandate of the Adonian Community;
# Declaring that the proposed personal sanctions against the Prime Minister of Okaiken, a head of government accountable to the Diet, would constitute an interference in the democratic processes of a member state in good standing, and are without precedent in the practice of the Community;
# Directing the Government to pursue the adoption of draft Resolution 4942D and to seek co-sponsorships among member states;
# Calling upon member states of the Adonian Community to withhold co-sponsorship from draft Resolution 4942E;
# Reaffirming that the abstention of 28 September 2026 on draft Resolution 4936 was a judgement on the merits of sanctions rather than a favour withheld, and that the Government will continue to vote on each draft according to its own assessment;
# Recording the gratitude of the House to the wounded seamen of the ''[[Aozora Maru]]'' and directing the continued protection of Sanese-flagged evacuation shipping.

== Debate ==

Foreign Minister [[Kenichi Mori]], opening for the government, described the Sindewand draft as "a prosecution brief in search of a crime" and defended the escort rules of engagement as the most restrained ever enacted by a member state: "Our destroyers may intercept shells already in the air and silence the battery that fired them. They may do nothing else. The Committee on Resolutions is invited to name the article of the Charter that a ferry violates."

[[Koichiro Sadanuma]] (LDP), whose party had moved a motion of no confidence against Mori two days earlier, led the opposition's support for the resolution: "This House spent the week examining the Government's failures, and it was right to do so. But when the Assembly is asked to sanction the Prime Minister of Okaiken for the sin of escorting ferries, the House is not divided, and the nation is not divided."

[[Ryota Endo]] (PPO) supported the resolution while placing responsibility for the confrontation on the government's diplomatic record: "We abstained on 4936 and called it principle. Sindewand heard it as a slap, and this is the return of serve. A foreign policy of gestures purchases exactly this." Endo's caucus split on the final vote, the largest bloc supporting the resolution while sixteen members abstained.

[[Kei Yamada]] (OIP) led the sole party opposition, arguing that the resolution would harden the Assembly's posture against Okaiken: "The fastest way to kill 4942E is to give it nothing to condemn. Recall the flotilla to Alwani transit waters, accept the Committee's jurisdiction, and the draft dies in committee. Instead, this House proposes to argue the Sindewand brief line by line in public."

[[Shimane Yoshida]] (SDP) closed the debate for the governing coalition, framing the statutory rules of engagement as the boundary of the "Yoshida–Ikazaki red line": "A shield that may not strike is not a weapon. This House built that shield by statute, in public, clause by clause. We will not apologise for it to any delegation."

