== Government response to 4942E ==

On the afternoon of the vote, the Sanese delegation to the Adonian Community lodged a formal written reply with the Committee on Resolutions, signed by Foreign Minister Mori. The reply advanced four points: that the deployment proceeded under the humanitarian mandate of Resolution 4935 and had been notified to the Assembly at its inception; that the rules of engagement were statutory, published, and strictly defensive, in contrast to the classified rules under which the coalition forces of the [[Joint Working Group for Peace in Northern Kaftia]] operated; that the proposed personal sanctions against a head of government accountable to a freely elected parliament were without precedent against a member state in good standing; and that Okaiken would appear before any hearing the Committee chose to convene.

The reply closed with an invitation: Sindewand was invited to co-sponsor draft Resolution 4942D, whose deconfliction zones would extend protection to all civilian shipping in the Pfein Sea regardless of flag. "A state concerned for the law of the sea has a draft before it that writes that law," the reply concluded. "Sindewand is welcome to sign it."

Prime Minister Ikazaki, asked at a press availability whether he would comply with the proposed asset freeze, replied: "I will not be lectured on international law by a state that closed its borders to the dying." The remark drew formal protest from the Sindewand delegation the following day; the Prime Minister's office declined to withdraw it.

Delegation diplomacy in the following week concentrated on the twenty-member co-sponsorship threshold. The delegations of the East Fosian Sphere partners were instructed to treat the draft's entry into discussion as the operative question, and the quiet maritime registries of the region — [[Ntungwe]] among them — were identified in diplomatic reporting as likely abstainers from any co-sponsorship list.

== Aftermath ==

The [[House of Officers of Okaiken]] adopted a concurrent resolution by voice vote on 28 October without amendment. The co-sponsorship diplomacy directed by the resolution bore fruit within days: between 28 and 29 October, Echia, Pavia, Tortona and Rufusia — the Echian block — acceded to the co-sponsorship of draft Resolution 4942D, followed by Kavik and the Vaiahi Islands, bringing its sponsors to nine while draft 4942E attracted none. The Committee on Resolutions continued to hold draft 4942E without discussion as of the end of October, while draft 4942D remained pending with its expanded co-sponsorship. The [[Okaiken Transport Workers' Union]] (OTWU) welcomed the resolution as "the seaman's answer to the prosecutor's brief," and the ''ISN Shirakumo'' continued its escort schedule under the statutory rules of engagement without further incidents of shore fire.

